  "body": "## What changed\n\nA rest operation no longer simulates the program ahead while it is staged. The staging runs on the session thread (MCP) or the UI thread (GUI). The simulation now runs in the generation job, on the worker thread.\n\n- `rest::prior_state` is split in two halves.\n- `rest::stage_prior` does all world reads: the chain of operations ahead, the digest and the stock grid. It keeps the order and the refusals of before.\n- `StagedPrior::simulate` cuts the cached moves ahead into the stock. It reads no world.\n- `collect_job` keeps the staged half in the new field `GenJob::prior_staged`.\n- `run_job` calls `GenJob::settle_prior` first. Thus the simulation runs on the job thread.\n- The corner-relief reader (`zones_for_op`) settles the grid before its WCS yaw turn reads it.\n- `prior_state` keeps its signature. It calls the two halves in sequence.\n\nThis covers 3D Pocket, Multi-Axis Rough, and a 2D Pocket or 2D Adaptive whose rest reads the previous operations.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #3860 moved the generator of an MCP `generate` to a worker thread. But `StagedGeneration::new` calls `collect_job` on the session thread. For a rest operation, `collect_job` called `rest::prior_state`, which simulated all operations ahead. On a large part, this blocked every other MCP call for that time. The issue comment of 2026-11-24 names this open part.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `generate_staged::a_rest_reading_pocket_simulates_the_program_ahead_in_its_job_not_at_staging`.\n  - It stages a 3D Pocket after a Face cut. It asserts that the staging thread simulates nothing.\n  - It finishes the job on a second thread and asserts one simulation there.\n  - It asserts that the path is equal to the path of the one-shot `GenerateOperation`.\n- Red before the fix: `assertion left == right failed: staging simulates nothing; left: 1, right: 0`.\n- Mutation: the simulation put back inside `stage` (the old timing) makes the pin red with the same message. With the fix restored, the pin is green.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green, 181 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (25.4 min).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Example catalog suites `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`: 46 passed, 0 failed (4 ignored by their own markers).\n- Light lane `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The change moves where the simulation runs, not what it computes. The example catalog suites ran green, and `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" examples/catalog` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The original QA mould core project is not on this machine. I did not measure the time on it.\n- A carried chain across setups (#318) stays eager on the staging thread. Its body comes from a per-thread cache. `docs/decisions/3035-rest-staging-worker.md` gives the reason.\n- The stock grid is still built at staging (`first_held` needs the world). It is an allocation, not a simulation.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. This is a `P3` PR (AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\").\n- No UI change, so no screenshots.\n\n## Open on #3035\n\n- The run time of the generators on the mould core.\n- A cancel point inside the generators.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/app/src/operation/job.rs` or `crates/app/src/rest.rs`.\n\nChangelog: A rest operation (3D Pocket, Multi-Axis Rough, rest 2D Pocket or 2D Adaptive) simulates the operations ahead in its background job, so MCP calls and the GUI stay responsive while it is staged.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3035#issuecomment-7200445799\n\nRefs #3035\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
